📝 Problem Statement & Functional Requirements

Transducer Acquisition:

Sample the analog temperature transducer on pin A0 continuously.
Map the 10-bit ADC reading (\(0 - 1023\)) to temperature: \(\text{Temp}(^\circ\text{C}) = \frac{\text{raw} \times 100.0}{1023.0}\).

Thermal State Decision Logic:

Safe State (&lt; 45.0°C): Green LED on D2 is ON, Red LED on D3 is OFF, and Buzzer on D5 is OFF.
Hazard State (&gt;= 45.0°C): Green LED is OFF, Red LED is ON, Buzzer pulses at 2 Hz (250 ms ON, 250 ms OFF), and send "[ALERT] OVERHEAT HAZARD: &lt;temp&gt; C" over UART at 115200 baud.

Non-Blocking Constraint: The buzzer pulse is driven using millis() timing comparisons.



